From 10ee2dc45e12f5ad18a78fdf5368fb9001f3a3b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: the speakers of the sound are told again
 after the audio engine clears them

The plane of the speakers on the Audio page of the player information said
"not known" for the whole video. ActiveAE::Configure() clears what the
player told Kodi's data cache of its stream whenever the engine's own
format changes (CDataCacheCore::ResetAudioCache()): its layout, rate, bits,
decoder and presentation. When the display changes its mode for a video
(Dolby Vision, with the ELD that changes with the mode), the first sink
cannot be opened, the engine opens it again a moment later for the stream,
its format changes, and the layout that the player had told is gone. The
player told it once, when the stream started, so hades.audio.spk stayed
empty. kodi.log of 1.0 and of the first builds of 1.1 shows that start ("failed to create
audio renderer", then the sink opened again) in 5 of 12 and 10 of 14
videos.

- CVideoPlayerAudio tells it again from its own copies (CProcessInfo and
  the presentation) where the cache has lost it (KeepStreamInfo(),
  StreamInfoCleared()), and kodi.log says so once a stream.
- A stream that the player synchronised while it was still starting
  (GENERAL_RESYNC in SYNC_STARTING) never took the step that tells it: it
  is told with its first frame that the output takes.
- The dialogue level sent in passthrough is told again the same way.
- Where what the player told names no speaker, the plane shows the usual
  layout of the stream's number of channels (Kodi's standard layouts, as
  CAEUtil::GuessChLayout() gives them), and a note under it says that it is
  that; kodi.log says, once a video, what the player had told where that
  lasts 3 s with the page open.
